  "problem_statement": "fix(sandbox): probe must actually run a container, not just query info\n\nCI was failing 4 live-container tests with 'crun: unknown version\nspecified' instead of skipping them. Root cause: runtime_available() ran\n'podman info' (which returns 0 even when the OCI runtime is broken) but\nnever tried to run a container, so the test skip-guard passed a false\npositive and the tests errored at run time.\n\nNow the probe runs a throwaway container from the configured image to\ncatch a broken OCI runtime -- but only when that image is already local\n(avoids blocking on a slow pull; falls back to the info check otherwise).\nResult cached for 60s so production sandbox-mode use doesn't pay the\nprobe cost per command. Added regression tests for the broken-runtime and\nimage-absent fallback paths.",
